WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.160
So You've probably heard about climate change
just about everywhere.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.799
But what exactly is climate change and global
warming?

00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:12.570
On a very basic level, it's the world heating
up.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:17.470
Climate change is a very complex beast, with
hundreds of factors, but let's talk about

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:22.850
the fundamental cause at the root at it all,
Carbon Dixoide, or CO2.

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:28.170
Carbon Dioxide is a naturally occurring gas,
it's inside us and everywhere around us, so

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.300
why is everyone so up in arms about it?

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.840
Well for hundreds of thousands of years the
CO2 levels in the atmosphere have been relatively

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.550
stable, hovering around 250 parts per million
(PPM).

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:44.750
But the industrial revolution in the past
few hundred years and the drastic increase

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:50.489
of fossil fuels being burnt has caused the
CO2 levels to shoot up to around 390 parts

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:51.489
per million (PPM).

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:56.430
This is bad because Carbon Dioxide behaves
like a greenhouse, letting heat from the sun

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:01.730
into the earth's atmosphere very easily, but
making it very hard for it to escape.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:06.329
Whilst CO2 is the biggest contributor to the
greenhouse effect, other gases come into play

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:07.520
as well.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:14.399
Methane, Nitrous Oxide and Chlorofluorocarbon
or "CFC", all of which have an effect on climate

00:01:14.399 --> 00:01:15.399
change.

00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:19.340
The biggest human cause of climate change
is the burning of fossil fuels to generate

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.689
energy, the same energy you use every time
you switch a light on.

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:26.979
65% of carbon emissions come from the burning
of fuels.

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:33.899
21% of carbon emissions come from transport,
7% comes from methane emissions from agricultural

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:35.700
livestock, going about their business.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.170
And the rest comes from various other sources.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:45.100
But here's the kicker, humans only contribute
around 0.28% of global greenhouse gases, the

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.310
rest comes from natural sources, such as volcanos
and the oceans.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:53.579
Of course they don't tell you that on the
news, because it's much less terrifying and

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.649
nobody would care about climate change.

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:59.850
But if human contributions are so small why
should we care?

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:05.709
Well the truth is 0.28% is terrifying, and
you have good reason to be worried.

00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:10.060
Since the formation of the earth greenhouse
gases have been in a fine balance, massive

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.660
amounts of gases, mostly methane, have been
constantly released from volcanic eruptions

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:20.470
for over 4.54 billion years, but most of these
harmful gases have been absorbed back into

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:24.210
the oceans, stopping any greenhouse effects
from kicking in and taking over.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:29.420
But in the short time humans have been emitting
greenhouse gases we have pushed the levels

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.190
over the edge, it's like a straw braking the
camel's back.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:39.420
That small 0.28% of greenhouse gases is enough
to send the CO2 levels into harmful amounts

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:43.360
resulting in exponentially increasing CO2
levels.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.400
Humans are producing more carbon than the
oceans can handle.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.180
The oceans can only absorb so much carbon,
so the remainder is sent into the atmosphere,

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.570
and when that happens, you're gonna have a
bad time.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:58.450
All these effects are compounded by the rapid
deforestation of the earth's rain forests.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:03.210
Since trees directly reverse the effects of
global warming, by taking in carbon dioxide

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:07.120
and releasing oxygen, through a process called
photosynthesis.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.430
The more trees we cut down, the less CO2 is
removed from the atmosphere and this results

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:20.970
in a vicious cycle and rapidly increasing
CO2 levels.

